# Every select in the main sources that races work its function started, judged: tools/check/select-races.py says what a
# site is and what each verdict means. <path> | <function> | <count> | <verdict> | <reason>. The question for each: when
# the started work and the other event are ready together, either clause may win; is each outcome right?
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/ClientRequestStream.kt | openUnlessGoAway | 1 | rechecked | a GOAWAY that wins cancels the open and awaits it: a stream the transport handed over all the same is reset and stopped, never left open (RFC 9114 section 5.2)
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.kt | withinWtDeadline | 1 | rechecked | the timer's side cancels and joins the block and returns its result when it completed all the same; WtDeadlineRaceTest forces both orders through the wtTimer hook
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.shutdown.kt | launchDrainer | 1 | seam | the drainer's reader calls a test hook through which the shutdown tests hold either side
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/RequestStream.kt | handOver | 1 | rechecked | the transport's end looks at the stream again: a stream that came whole has its flush cancelled (nothing is taken from anyone), otherwise the flush is joined; a flush that won left nothing to undo
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | open | 1 | rechecked | a session close that wins cancels the opening, and a stream it opened all the same is reset and stopped once the opening completes (invokeOnCompletion), keeping its header (section 4.4)
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | httpsUpgrade | 1 | rechecked | the select only ends the first wait; the HTTPS query's state is read again after it (isCompleted, then the extra wait or the secure source's join), so an answer that came with the addresses is used
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | awaitResolutions | 1 | rechecked | the select only ends the first wait; each resolution's state is read again after it (outcome checks isCompleted), so a record that came with the addresses is used
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | track | 1 | both-alike | the exchange's end and the connection's end both lead to the same cancel and release of the session's slot
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/H2c.kt | startsWithH2PrefaceUnless | 1 | rechecked | a stop that wins cancels and joins the preface check, then reads the octets already in without waiting: a whole preface that came with the stop is served as HTTP/2 and ended with GOAWAY (RFC 9113 sections 3.3, 6.8), a partial or other one goes to HTTP/1.1; H2PrefaceDrainRaceTest forces the stop through h2cPrefaceCheckForTest
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/Http2Serving.kt | serveH2 | 1 | tested-each | a stop that wins sends GOAWAY naming the last stream the core took and serves those, a preface that wins leaves the stop to the draining watcher (two-step GOAWAY, the streams taken finish); H2PrefaceDrainRaceTest.negative_aRequestTakenAsTheStopWinsIsServedOverH2c and H2PrefaceDrainRaceTest.negative_aRequestTakenAsThePrefaceWinsIsServedOverH2c force each outcome with stream 1 taken (TLS twins too)
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/HeadLimitedInput.kt | awaitSource | 1 | both-alike | a gate that wins cancels the wait without taking bytes, and the next wait under the body deadline reads the source the same way; bytes that came with the gate are read there
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/ServerPipeline.kt | awaitRequestStart | 1 | seam | requestStartForTest inside the wait for the head; H1PipelineSelectRaceTest forces each side, and the stop's side rechecks the input, so a head that came with the stop is answered
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/ServerPipeline.kt | startH1Pipeline | 1 | seam | bodyReadForTest inside the body read; H1PipelineSelectRaceTest forces each side, and a complete body keeps the connection either way (settleUnreadBody returns the reader's outcome)
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/ServerPipeline.kt | lingerAfterRefusal | 1 | both-alike | the linger ends either when the input is drained or when the server stops; the connection is closed next either way and the discard is cancelled
